Subject: [PATCH] feat(skills): add worktree and gates triggering skills

Two previously skill-less features (worktree lifecycle, gate/rail
toggling) now have full triggering skills with descriptions, router
entries, and eval fixtures, and are un-exempted in the coverage map.

- skills/worktree: forge worktree create/list/remove + forge clean;
  footgun (raw git worktree add misses issue-link + deps), cwd-scope,
  Windows long-path cleanup. Router keywords + 6 should_trigger /
  3 should_not fixtures. desc-quality 100.
- skills/gates: forge gate enable/disable/approve/reject/status/check +
  forge control; default-ON toggleable rails (tdd_intent, kernel_tracking,
  auto_shepherd); disable makes hooks genuinely inert. Router keywords +
  6 should_trigger / 3 should_not fixtures. desc-quality 100.
- coverage.json: worktree+clean -> worktree; gate+control+doc-gate ->
  gates. orphans corrected to issue-basics (it is forge issue orphans,
  a dangling-dependency-edge command, not worktree cleanup).
- .agents mirror regenerated by sync-agent-skills hook.

Coverage gate PASS (0 gaps); worktree/gate now MAPPED. 303 tests green.

